## 3. Design rules: “Hungry competition” without predatory vibes

Here’s a table you can treat as your ethics + Google-safe blueprint:

### Table – Pillars for ethical “advance” design

| Pillar                                      | What you do                                                                                                              | Why it’s ethical & Google-friendly                                                                                            | Design DOs                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                            | Design DON’Ts                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                      |
| ------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |
| 1. All in-game, no real finance             | Keep everything in soft currency, hard currency, and game items only. No real-money APR, no “repay in 30 days” language. | Keeps you out of the **personal loan** policy zone. You’re just another F2P game with challenges & passes. ([Google Help][4]) | – Only talk about *challenges*, *contracts*, and *rewards*.<br>– Use gems/gold as optional settlement, never real-world interest.<br>– Make gem fees small vs normal shop prices (feels like a discount, not punishment).<br>– Show all gem/soft costs up front. No surprises.<br>– Keep “Advance Challenges” separate from normal cash offers.                                       | – Don’t call it loans/credit/APR in-game or on your store page.<br>– Don’t tie any of this to external credit cards or BNPL APIs.<br>– Don’t imply “you owe us real money if you fail.”<br>– Don’t set repayment deadlines like “within 30 days” in a financial tone.<br>– Don’t add any real-world interest or fees.                                              |
| 2. Transparency & no dark patterns          | Always show: what you got, what you must do, by when, what happens if you fail. No hidden conditions, no trick buttons.  | Deceptive UX (“dark patterns”) can be considered deceptive behavior, which Google bans. ([Google Play][1])                    | – Single clear screen: **“Here’s your Advance”** with 4 bullets (Rewards, Goal, Deadline, Outcomes).<br>– Big progress bar on home screen that updates live.<br>– Remind players (non-annoyingly) as the deadline approaches.<br>– Give a free “test mini contract” so players learn the system risk-free.<br>– Make “No thanks” / “Cancel” equally visible and easy to tap.          | – Don’t bury the fail condition in tiny text or extra menus.<br>– Don’t use misleading CTAs like “Continue” that really mean “Buy”. ([rainintelligence.com][5]) <br>– Don’t hide the gem fee until the final step.<br>– Don’t auto-opt players into contracts.<br>– Don’t add guilt or shaming messages (“Cowards cancel contracts”).                              |
