## 4. Concrete wording: what the player actually sees

### Good “ethical competition” version

> **Advance Gold Pass – Season Challenge**
>
> You get **Gold Pass rewards unlocked now**:
> • Premium reward track active
> • Extra daily quests
> • Exclusive tower skin (provisional)
>
> **Complete this challenge by Season End (28 days):**
> • Reach **Gold League** *or* win **80 battles**
>
> **If you succeed:**
> • All Gold Pass rewards stay permanently on your account
> • Your **Advance Level** increases (better offers next season)
>
> **If you don’t:**
> • You keep everything you already claimed on the free track
> • Choose one:
> – Pay **250 Gems** to keep your Gold Pass progress, or
> – Let your tower skin revert & lose the last 5 premium tiers
>
> This is an **optional challenge**. You can play the whole season without it.

Notice:

* It never says “loan,” “debt,” “interest,” “repayment.”
* It’s obviously a **game challenge** with a clear goal and clear outcomes.
* There’s an option to **walk away**.

### Bad / dangerous version (what *not* to do)

> **Limited Time Loan – Premium Pass on Credit**
>
> You receive a **$15 value loan** of Premium Pass content.
> APR: **“Variable”**, repayment in **30 days**.
>
> Failure to reach Diamond League will incur **penalty interest**.
> If you cannot repay, your account will be restricted until your **balance is cleared** with real money.

This screams “financial product” + debt + coercion, which is exactly what gets loan apps and manipulative monetization in trouble. ([Wccftech][6])

